# ADR-0313 (F-09, F-68), ADR-0342 item 4: a HELLO without a usable
# user_agent — here the empty string, which the session treats as absent —
# is rejected and opens no session; the RESET after it is IGNORED; a second
# HELLO is a breach in the AUTHENTICATION state and the server closes. The
# absent-user_agent variant is pinned by hello-absent-user-agent.bolt: one
# connection holds at most one rejected HELLO.
!: BOLT 4.4

C: HELLO {"user_agent": "", "scheme": "none"}
S: FAILURE {"code": "Neo.ClientError.Request.Invalid", "message": "Illegal value for field \"user_agent\": Expected value to be non-null"}
C: RESET
S: IGNORED
C: HELLO {"user_agent": "relate-bolt-compat/1.0", "scheme": "none"}
S: FAILURE {"code": "Neo.ClientError.Request.Invalid", "message": "*"}
S: <EXIT>
